This file is the next git commit message (`git commit -F`). Keep it cumulative.

Agents: **append** a short why after each slice of work. Prefix each WIP
line (or paragraph) with a source credit:

  [c]   Cursor agent
  [oc]  OpenCode agent
  [h]   human (optional)

Do not replace the whole file with only the latest turn.

After a human runs commit.sh, the file becomes `committed <timestamp>`. The next
WIP should replace that stamp (or write below it).

Agents: do not run commit.sh or git mutations unless the human grants permission.

Example:
[c] Land fleet SSH so Cursor keeps one Host thin_host while LAN/ZT is only TCP.
[oc] Fix sidebar overflow on dialogue studio.
